      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1753, a young George Washington passed through what is now Cranberry Twp while delivering a message that contributed to the French and Indian War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cranberry_Township%2C_Butler_County%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cranberry Twp was primarily an agricultural community until the completion of the Pennsylvania Turnpike's western section in 1951, which spurred its growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
